    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Ravi made bigger and bigger squares using matchsticks.\n\"How many sticks for the 10th square?\" he asked."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "pattern",
     "rule",
     "generalise"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Shapes can grow in patterns. A row of squares made from matchsticks uses 4, 7, 10, 13 sticks, adding 3 each time.\nFrom the pattern we can find a rule: for n squares in a row we need 3 times n plus 1 sticks.\nSo 10 squares need 3 times 10 plus 1, which is 31 sticks."
    }
   },
